From af64eccefceea05bc18047c87b8a3a6cf745127a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MINJUN GIL <alswnsrlf12@naver.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:40:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0014e-b70-offload-group-evict: backport vllm#51787
 request-scoped recency / tail-before-head eviction (UNGATED)

Backport of upstream f12fe10c5c ([KV Offload] per-request recency, merged to
vllm main 2026-09-16; not in our v0.30.0 base ced6857afa). Applied from the PR
diff; it applied cleanly on the base and auto-merged over 0014a-d.

The scheduler no longer touches keys on every lookup/store; the CPU manager
records the keys a request loaded or offered, with their token positions, and
applies one logical head-to-tail access in on_request_finished. The LRU policy
keeps logical recency separate from transfer pinning, so eviction runs tail
before head across all KV groups of a request, including the hybrid Mamba/GDN
groups (a lone GDN checkpoint is no longer evicted independently of the
full-attention chunks at the same position).

NOT env-gated: it replaces the LRU policy's data structure and removes the
scheduler's per-step touch; a gate would need both implementations side by
side. An engine carrying 0014 therefore differs from the serving engine in
eviction policy regardless of the B70_OFFLOAD_* flags.

(cherry picked from commit f12fe10c5c, vllm-project/vllm#51787)
